---
import FeatureCard from '@chassis-ui/docs/components/FeatureCard.astro'
import Code from '@chassis-ui/docs/shortcodes/Code.astro'

// A repository of icons that `init` wrote, after a first build
const tree = `acme-icons/
├── source/
│   ├── bar-line.svg
│   └── ...
├── package.json
├── codepoints.json
├── README.md
└── dist/`

const archives = `acme-icons-web-<version>.zip
acme-icons-ios-<version>.zip
acme-icons-android-<version>.zip`
---

<section class="home-section py-3xl md:py-6xl">
  <div class="container 2xl section-content">
    <div class="grid mb-3xl md:mb-6xl">
      <header class="section-header col-span-full lg:col-span-10 lg:col-start-2 xl:col-span-8 xl:col-start-3 text-center">
        <h2 class="section-title font-3xl md:font-4xl lg:font-5xl mb-xs md:mb-sm lg:mb-md">
          <span class="font-normal d-block">From SVG files</span> to a release
        </h2>
        <p class="section-body md:font-lg lg:font-xl m-0">
          The repository that <code>init</code> writes has a script for each command, a CI workflow
          and a release workflow. The commands here are those of npm, and{' '}
          <code>init --pm pnpm</code> writes them for pnpm.
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="section-features grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-md md:gap-xl">
      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-one">
          <Fragment slot="title">Save the icons</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Save one SVG file per icon into <code>source/</code>, drawn on the frame of the set in
            one color. The build only reads this folder.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md">
            <Code noToolbar lang="text" code={tree} />
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-two">
          <Fragment slot="title">Build the set</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            The build writes <code>dist/</code>, and beside it <code>codepoints.json</code>,{' '}
            <code>README.md</code> and the fields of <code>package.json</code> that name the files.
            Commit those with <code>source/</code>. <code>dist/</code> is not committed.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md">
            <Code
              noToolbar
              lang="bash"
              code={`npm run lint
npm run build
npm run verify`}
            />
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>

      <div>
        <FeatureCard icon="cx-number-three">
          <Fragment slot="title">Release a version</Fragment>
          <Fragment slot="body">
            Push a new version with its entry in <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> to <code>main</code>. The
            release workflow builds <code>dist/</code> again, publishes the package to npm for the
            web, and attaches an archive per target to the GitHub release. The web archive holds the
            page of the set.
          </Fragment>
          <div class="border-top border-subtle pt-md">
            <Code noToolbar lang="text" code={archives} />
          </div>
        </FeatureCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
